ORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPS-030", "label": "Study family SF-APPS-030: Coaching alignment: BEST/AVOID run rates vs series wins (55 series)", "score": 0.765, "reached_via": ["request matches the question or hypothesis of FAM:SF-APPS-030 (0.77)"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Coaching alignment: BEST/AVOID run rates vs series wins (55 series)", "auto_outcome_status": "untestable", "observed_hypothesis": "Teams that run BEST counters more (and AVOID less) after suppression win more series.", "observed_result": "% ran BEST 44.7% of triggers / 9.7% volume; % ran AVOID 61.1% / 23.3% volume. Spearman BEST vs won rho=+0.131 p=0.1723; AVOID vs won rho=-0.098 p=0.3099. Mean PPP BEST 1.395 vs AVOID 0.865.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Alignment-win Spearmans ns (p=0.172 / 0.310) at n=110 directions; INSUFF_EVIDENCE is 91.5% of triggers.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=110 series-directions", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null", "observed_failure_type": "A_unanswerable"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF05"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPM-054", "label": "Study family SF-APPM-054: Playoff adaptation-pair sustainability (12 pairs x 74 matchups)", "score": 0.755, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPM-055 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPM-054", "request matches RQC:RQC-021 (0.75); FAM:SF-APPM-054 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-021"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Playoff adaptation-pair sustainability (12 pairs x 74 matchups)", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Pivoting to a listed counter after suppression sustains higher PPP than not pivoting, consistently across playoff matchups.", "observed_result": "10/12 pairs CONSISTENT and within 0.10 of non-pivot (no PIVOT_WINS). PNR->PULL_UP sustained 1.069 vs non_pivot 1.224 (n_matchups=9) PIVOT_LOSES. DRIVE->PULL_UP 1.101 vs 1.217 (n=5) PIVOT_LOSES. Largest positive pair in t [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Population deltas mostly |d|<0.10; two pairs with enough signal are PIVOT_LOSES (pivot worse than staying).", "observed_sample_and_power": "n=74 matchups; pair n_matchups 5 to 44"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}, {"rel": "auto_related_family", "node": "FAM:SF-APPM-033"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-058", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-058: Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "score": 0.476, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-051 (0.76); FAM:SF-APPA-058 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-051"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Season stability of top suppressors and negative teammate pairs", "auto_outcome_status": "rejected", "observed_hypothesis": "Each star's top sequential suppressor is stable across seasons, and some teammate X->Y sequences have large negative premiums.", "observed_result": "2/30 (7%) stable (>=75% same top suppressor): D. Mitchell PUTBACK 75%, L. James POST_UP 75%. Negative: J. Tatum->K. Porzingis DRIVE->SPOT_UP -0.444 n=31; Giannis->Lillard DRIVE->PNR -0.263 n=31; J. Brown->J. Tatum SPOT_U [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "B_powered_null (adequately powered null result)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Only 2/30 stars meet the 75% same-top-suppressor stability rule.", "observed_sample_and_power": "30 stars x 4 seasons; min n=20/cell", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_verdict": "null"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:small_sample"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-CHT-009", "label": "Study family SF-CHT-009: Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "score": 0.476, "reached_via": ["request matches RQC:RQC-096 (0.75); FAM:SF-CHT-009 auto_addresses_question RQC:RQC-096"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Superstar suppression by lineup and forced play type", "auto_outcome_status": "not a hypothesis test", "observed_hypothesis": "Named star initiators have identifiable lineup and forced-play-type suppressors in the possession graph.", "observed_result": "Jokic vs MIN lineup PPP 0.814, -0.385 (n=59); Curry vs HOU 0.851, -0.358 (n=47); Doncic vs LAC 0.733, -0.396 (n=30); Giannis forced PULL_UP 0.848, -0.540 vs preferred DRIVE (largest gap).", "auto_failure_mechanism": "E_unclear (mechanism unclear from the records)", "observed_failure_evidence": "No placebo or matching; later sequence work treated similar star-chain gaps as artifacts.", "observed_sample_and_power": "n>=30 for lineup cells cited", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED", "observed_method": "Jokic/Curry/Doncic/Giannis; min-15 gate on 8 play types; opposing DEFENSE_LINEUP ~84% coverage; 272-row CSV."}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:PLACEBO_DEPENDENCE"}]}], "n_results": 10}

